<!-- ============================================================
     Void Stealer: Steam C2 Resolution + Browser Credential Theft
     MITRE ATT&CK Techniques:
       T1102      - Web Service (Steam profile for C2 server address resolution)
       T1555.003  - Credentials from Web Browsers
       T1528      - Steal Application Access Token (Discord token theft)
       T1071.001  - Application Layer Protocol: Web Protocols
     Rule IDs: 103919-103924
     Author: SecOps Engineer
     Date: 2026-07-14

     Threat Actor: Multiple affiliates (Malware-as-a-Service on Telegram)
     References:
       - SOCRadar (2026): Void Stealer MaaS infostealer analysis
       - F5 Labs Weekly Threat Bulletin July 8, 2026
       - IOC: citrusshop.icu (C2), SteamID 76561199877608270 (C2 resolution)

     Threat Summary:
       Void Stealer is a Windows infostealer distributed as Malware-as-a-Service
       with up to 6 simultaneous affiliate campaigns. Notable techniques:
         - C2 resolution via Steam gaming profile: rather than hardcoding a server
           address, the binary queries a Steam profile (SteamID 76561199877608270)
           whose display name encodes the current C2 IP/domain (T1102)
         - Syscall bypass: resolves NTAPI calls directly from ntdll.dll at runtime
           to evade EDR user-mode hooks (T1562.006)
         - Browser credential theft via headless browser automation:
           Chrome/Edge/Firefox spawned with -no-sandbox -disable-extensions
           -window-position=-32000,-32000 (moves off-screen to hide window)
         - Discord token theft from AppData\Roaming\discord\Local Storage
         - Telegram session file theft from AppData\Roaming\Telegram Desktop\tdata

     IOC Domains/IDs:
       citrusshop.icu                   (Void Stealer primary C2)
       steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199877608250  (C2 address resolution)

     Log source prerequisites:
       - Firewall/network logs via 103000 anchor
         Required for C2 domain detection (103919) and Steam C2 resolution (103920)
       - Sysmon EventID 1 (ProcessCreate) -> Wazuh SID 61603
         Required for headless browser credential harvest (103921)
         Required for browser profile path access (103922)
         Required for Discord token access (103923)
       - Frequency rule parent (103924) requires 103922 firing

     Severity tiers:
       12 - Non-browser process reading browser profile paths (may have FP)
       12 - Discord Local Storage access by non-Discord process
       13 - Browser spawned with -window-position=-32000,-32000 (off-screen)
       14 - Direct C2 domain IOC or Steam profile C2 resolution
       14 - Multiple browser profile accesses in rapid succession
     ============================================================ -->

<group name="threat_intel,credential_access,windows,void_stealer,infostealer,">

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Network: outbound connection to citrusshop.icu (Void Stealer C2)
       citrusshop.icu is the confirmed primary C2 for Void Stealer.
       Connections to this domain indicate active C2 communication.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="103919" level="14">
    <if_sid>103000</if_sid>
    <match>citrusshop.icu</match>
    <description>Void Stealer: connection to confirmed C2 domain citrusshop.icu from $(agent.name) -- Void Stealer MaaS infostealer active C2 communication; browser credentials and Discord tokens at risk (T1071.001, T1555.003)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1071.001</id>
      <id>T1555.003</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>ioc_match,ioc_domain,ioc_c2,void_stealer,critical,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Network: Void Stealer querying Steam profile for C2 resolution
       Void Stealer resolves its C2 server address by querying the Steam
       community profile of SteamID 76561199877608270 and parsing the
       display name field. Outbound connections to steamcommunity.com from
       non-gaming contexts (servers, workstations with no Steam installed)
       warrant investigation. Rule fires on any hit containing the known
       SteamID in network traffic or DNS queries.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="103920" level="12">
    <if_sid>103000</if_sid>
    <match>steamcommunity.com</match>
    <match>76561199877608270</match>
    <description>Void Stealer: Steam profile query for SteamID 76561199877608270 (Void Stealer C2 resolution) from $(agent.name) -- Void Stealer resolves C2 server address from Steam profile display name (T1102)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1102</id>
      <id>T1071.001</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>ioc_match,steam_c2,void_stealer,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Sysmon EventID 1 (61603): Browser spawned off-screen for credential harvest
       Void Stealer spawns Chrome/Edge/Firefox in headless-like mode to extract
       saved passwords. The -window-position=-32000,-32000 flag moves the window
       far off-screen to hide it from the user. Combined with -no-sandbox and
       -disable-extensions this is a near-unique Void Stealer behavioral fingerprint.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="103921" level="13">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" type="pcre2">(?i)\\(chrome|msedge|firefox|brave|opera|vivaldi)\.exe$</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.commandLine" type="pcre2">(?i)-window-position=-32000,-32000</field>
    <description>Void Stealer: browser $(win.eventdata.image) spawned with off-screen positioning (-window-position=-32000,-32000) on $(win.eventdata.computer) -- Void Stealer headless browser credential harvesting technique (T1555.003)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1555.003</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>credential_access,browser_harvest,void_stealer,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Sysmon EventID 1 (61603): Non-browser process accessing browser profile paths
       Void Stealer directly reads Chrome/Edge/Firefox credential stores from
       the user profile directory. Detecting non-browser processes opening these
       paths catches credential theft before network exfiltration occurs.
       Some legitimate tools (password managers, sync clients) may trigger FP -
       tune per environment.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="103922" level="12">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.commandLine" type="pcre2">(?i)(\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Default\\Login Data|\\Microsoft\\Edge\\User Data\\Default\\Login Data|\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Profiles\\.*\\logins\.json|\\BraveSoftware\\Brave-Browser\\User Data\\Default\\Login Data)</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" negate="yes" type="pcre2">(?i)\\(chrome|msedge|firefox|brave|opera|vivaldi|SearchIndexer|MsMpEng)\.exe$</field>
    <description>Void Stealer: non-browser process $(win.eventdata.image) accessing browser credential store on $(win.eventdata.computer) -- infostealer credential harvesting from browser profile (T1555.003)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1555.003</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>credential_access,browser_harvest,void_stealer,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Sysmon EventID 1 (61603): Discord Local Storage access by non-Discord process
       Void Stealer targets Discord authentication tokens stored in
       AppData\Roaming\discord\Local Storage\leveldb. Non-Discord processes
       accessing this path are performing Discord token theft.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="103923" level="12">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.commandLine" type="pcre2">(?i)\\discord\\Local Storage</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" negate="yes" type="pcre2">(?i)\\Discord(Setup|Updater|\.exe|PTB\.exe|Canary\.exe)?$</field>
    <description>Void Stealer: non-Discord process $(win.eventdata.image) accessing Discord Local Storage on $(win.eventdata.computer) -- Discord authentication token theft (T1528)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1528</id>
      <id>T1555.003</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>credential_access,token_theft,discord,void_stealer,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Frequency: multiple browser profile credential stores accessed in 60s
       Void Stealer sweeps across all installed browsers in rapid succession.
       Three or more browser profile accesses by the same non-browser process
       within 60 seconds indicates an active credential sweep.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="103924" level="14" frequency="3" timeframe="60">
    <if_matched_sid>103922</if_matched_sid>
    <same_field>win.eventdata.image</same_field>
    <description>Void Stealer: BROWSER CREDENTIAL SWEEP -- 3+ browser profile credential stores accessed in 60s by $(win.eventdata.image) on $(win.eventdata.computer) -- active multi-browser credential harvesting sweep (T1555.003)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1555.003</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>credential_access,browser_harvest,void_stealer,critical,</group>
  </rule>

</group>
